{"name":"Butterscotch Cake","hex":"#f1c882","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"butterscotch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard candy made from butter, brown sugar, syrup and vanilla.","A sauce or syrup made of similar ingredients."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a light brown colour, like that of butterscotch candy.","Having the flavour of butterscotch."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/butterscotch"},{"term":"cake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rich, sweet dessert food, typically made of flour, sugar, and eggs and baked in an oven, and often covered in icing.","A small mass of baked dough, especially a thin loaf from unleavened dough."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Coat (something) with a crust of solid material.","To form into a cake, or mass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Butterscotch","blocks":[{"text":"Butterscotch is a type of confection whose primary ingredients are brown sugar and butter. Some recipes include cream, vanilla, and salt. The earliest known recipes, in mid-19th century Yorkshire, used treacle (molasses) in place of, or in addition to, sugar."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Butterscotch-Candies.jpg/330px-Butterscotch-Candies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butterscotch","wikidata":"Q2009326"},{"title":"Cake","blocks":[{"text":"Cake is a baker's confectionery made by combining flour with a liquid, a fat or both, and usually with a leavening agent. Cakes are usually baked, but can be griddled. In their oldest forms, cakes were modifications of bread, but cakes now cover a wide range of preparations that can be simple or elaborate and which share features with other desserts such as pastries, meringues, custards, and pies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Pound_layer_cake.jpg/330px-Pound_layer_cake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cake","wikidata":"Q13276"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Rye_%2815045370394%29.jpg/500px-Rye_%2815045370394%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Rye_%2815045370394%29.jpg/1280px-Rye_%2815045370394%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Rye_%2815045370394%29.jpg/500px-Rye_%2815045370394%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Butterscotch sweets (top row second from left) sold in a shop in Rye, East Sussex, England","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARye_(15045370394).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Butterscotchsundae.jpg/500px-Butterscotchsundae.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Butterscotchsundae.jpg/1280px-Butterscotchsundae.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Butterscotchsundae.jpg/500px-Butterscotchsundae.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A butterscotch sundae","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AButterscotchsundae.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Bartolom%C3%A9_Esteban_Perez_Murillo_-_Baking_of_Flat_Cakes_-_WGA16350.jpg/500px-Bartolom%C3%A9_Esteban_Perez_Murillo_-_Baking_of_Flat_Cakes_-_WGA16350.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Bartolom%C3%A9_Esteban_Perez_Murillo_-_